WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
LiteRev turns a research question into an evidence-backed, predictive scenario. Here is the main pipeline, step by step.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.700
Ask
Write the research question in plain words or as a Boolean query. With live sources ticked, one search federates PubMed, OpenAlex, Europe PMC, Crossref and seven more databases.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:15.900
Every search becomes a scenario
Its corpus is deduplicated across sources and saved, ready to be screened, synthesised and kept up to date.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:26.800
Score and select
Each article gets a semantic relevance score. The threshold decides which articles feed the analyses. Those below it are kept, never deleted.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.100
Read and decide
Open an article to read its abstract and its PICO, then include or exclude it, with a reason.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:42.400
Screen the PRISMA way
The PRISMA 2020 flow counts every step: records per source, duplicates, AI pre-screening, human decisions and the final evidence set.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:51.000
Synthesise the whole corpus
Study designs, sources and GRADE levels are computed over every relevant article. The narrative brief and its PDF are written over this digest.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.300
One extraction per article
Population, intervention, comparator, outcome and main finding are extracted once per article, then aggregated over the whole corpus, never over a sample.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:03.500
Explore the literature
Topic clusters show what the corpus is made of. Select a group to narrow the corpus to it.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:11.300
Map concepts and gaps
The concept map links pathogens, exposures, outcomes and places, and lists the pairs that no study has examined together.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.200
From evidence to a model
The variables the literature points to become a model specification. Plug in real data, and train.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:24.200
Train, explain, monitor
The trained model reports its accuracy, its drivers and its guardrails, and raises an alert when a prediction crosses its threshold.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.100
Keep it living
Subscribe to alerts. The living review queries PubMed on a schedule and adds the new articles to the scenario.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.300
This video is generated by code from the real interface, so it is rebuilt whenever the interface changes.
